<!--meta {"lead": "The page header opens every screen: a short eyebrow, the page's one <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>, a subtitle with the facts that matter, and optional page actions.", "description": "Eyebrow, display h1, subtitle and actions; actions drop below the title and the primary goes full width on phones.", "pills": ["Holds the page <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "title only, with eyebrow and subtitle, with actions", "states": "static; actions follow button states", "sources": ["pages/style-gallery/default", "pages/appointment-detail/default", "pages/my-appointments/default", "pages/sign-in/default", "pages/not-found/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Every product page uses one page header as the first thing in <code>&lt;main&gt;</code> (after an optional <a href="breadcrumb.html">breadcrumb</a>). It holds the page's only <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> in the light display face, which carries HairPop's voice: "Find a style that feels like you", "Your appointment with Nia".</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The <b>eyebrow</b> names the area: "Discover" for browsing screens, the area name ("Appointments", "Account") for account screens.</li>
    <li>The <b>subtitle</b> carries the facts the customer checks first: "Request HP-1048 · Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am · awaiting Nia’s reply."</li>
    <li><b>Actions</b> are page-level only, with one primary at most; actions about one card stay in that card.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure" style="place-items: stretch;">
      <div class="page-header" style="margin: 0;"><div><p class="eyebrow">Appointments</p><h2 style="font: var(--text-h1); letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);">My appointments</h2><p class="subtitle">1 request awaiting a reply · 1 completed appointment.</p></div><div class="page-header__actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Book a style</a></div></div>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 4%; top: 16%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 4%; top: 40%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 4%; top: 70%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 92%; top: 70%;" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Eyebrow</b><small><code>.eyebrow</code>: overline, uppercase, wide tracking, <code>--color-fg-accent</code>, 8px above the title.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Title</b><small>The page <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>: <code>--text-h1</code> (light, fluid 40–68px), tight tracking, balanced wrapping.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Subtitle</b><small><code>.subtitle</code>: body text, <code>--color-fg-muted</code>, 4px below the title, capped at 65ch.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Actions (optional)</b><small><code>.page-header__actions</code>: at the end of the row, aligned to the bottom of the title block from 768px.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <p>Examples on this page use an <code>&lt;h2&gt;</code> styled as the title because this documentation page already has its own <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>; product pages always use <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack]With eyebrow and subtitle, the most common form (style gallery).}}
<div class="page-header" style="margin: 0;"><div><p class="eyebrow">Discover</p><h2 style="font: var(--text-h1); letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);">Find a style that feels like you</h2><p class="subtitle">Browse protective styles, compare typical time and price, and see real work.</p></div></div>
  {{/example}}
  {{example:[stack]With actions: one secondary and one primary, page-level only.}}
<div class="page-header" style="margin: 0;"><div><p class="eyebrow">Appointments</p><h2 style="font: var(--text-h1); letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);">Your appointment with Nia</h2><p class="subtitle">Request HP-1048 · Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am · awaiting Nia’s reply.</p></div><div class="page-header__actions"><a class="btn" href="../../mocks/dialogs/change-appointment/default.html">Request a change</a><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html">Message Nia</a></div></div>
  {{/example}}
  {{example:[stack]Title only, for legal pages where an eyebrow adds nothing.}}
<div class="page-header" style="margin: 0;"><div><h2 style="font: var(--text-h1); letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);">Terms of use</h2></div></div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="One size. The title scales fluidly with the viewport through --font-size-4xl (40–68px); nothing else changes."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>The header is static. Its actions follow the <a href="button.html#states">button states</a>. While the page loads, the header stays real (it does not become a skeleton) because its copy is known before the data arrives.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Active</th><th scope="col">Disabled</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Primary action</th><td><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html">Message Nia</a></td><td><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html" data-state="hover">Message Nia</a></td><td><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html" data-state="focus">Message Nia</a></td><td><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html" data-state="active">Message Nia</a></td><td><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" disabled>Message Nia</button></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Secondary action</th><td><a class="btn" href="../../mocks/dialogs/change-appointment/default.html">Request a change</a></td><td><a class="btn" href="../../mocks/dialogs/change-appointment/default.html" data-state="hover">Request a change</a></td><td><a class="btn" href="../../mocks/dialogs/change-appointment/default.html" data-state="focus">Request a change</a></td><td><a class="btn" href="../../mocks/dialogs/change-appointment/default.html" data-state="active">Request a change</a></td><td><button class="btn" type="button" disabled>Request a change</button></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<div class="page-header" style="margin: 0;"><div><p class="eyebrow">Discover</p><h2 style="font: var(--text-h2); letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);">Braiders for knotless braids</h2><p class="subtitle">12 braiders offer this style near Toronto.</p></div></div>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Below 768px</b>: actions move below the subtitle and take the full width; secondary actions come first and the primary, placed last in the markup, is full width on its own row. The visual order, the DOM order and the focus order stay the same at every width.</li>
    <li><b>From 768px</b>: actions keep their natural width and sit at the end of the row, aligned to the bottom of the title block, when the title leaves room; a title that fills the row pushes them onto the next line, left-aligned.</li>
    <li>With no actions the empty <code>.page-header__actions</code> takes no space (<code>:empty</code> is hidden).</li>
    <li>At 200% text a long title word breaks across lines (<code>overflow-wrap: anywhere</code>, <code>hyphens: auto</code>) rather than widening the page.</li>
    <li>The title is fluid (40px at 360px, 68px from about 1280px) and wraps with <code>text-wrap: balance</code>; keep it under about 40 characters so it fits in two lines on phones.</li>
    <li>24px (<code>--space-6</code>) separates the header from the page content at every width.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The header reads <code>--text-h1</code>, <code>--color-fg-default</code>, <code>--color-fg-accent</code> (eyebrow) and <code>--color-fg-muted</code> (subtitle). In the dark theme the eyebrow becomes plum 300 and the subtitle grey 350 on the grey 950 canvas. A brand theme changes the display family through <code>--font-family-display</code>, never the header rules.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>No ARIA. The title is the page's single <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>, and the document <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> starts with the same words ("My appointments — HairPop"). The eyebrow is a paragraph before the heading, not part of it, so the heading reads cleanly in a headings list.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>The header itself is not focusable; Tab reaches its actions in DOM order, which matches the visual order at every width.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Activates an action.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The skip link targets <code>&lt;main id="main"&gt;</code>, which starts with this header. After a client-side route change, move focus to the <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> (with <code>tabindex="-1"</code>) so screen-reader users hear the new page; the heading shows no ring because it is not a control. On a full page load focus is not moved and starts at the skip link.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The title names the page specifically ("Your appointment with Nia", not "Details"). Uppercase eyebrows are styled with CSS (<code>text-transform</code>), so screen readers read "Discover", not letter by letter.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Eyebrow on page|--color-fg-accent|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Title on page|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Subtitle on page|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>None.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Actions follow the button rules; on phones the full-width primary is at least 40px tall, and 48px when it is the screen's main action.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Titles are warm and specific, in sentence case, without a full stop: "Find a style that feels like you", "Care for your knotless braids".</li>
    <li>Subtitles hold facts separated by middle dots and end with a full stop: "Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am · awaiting Nia’s reply."</li>
    <li>Eyebrows are one or two words: "Discover" for browsing, the area name for account screens ("Appointments", "Account"), none for auth, legal, help and error pages.</li>
    <li>Never call a pending request "confirmed" in the title or subtitle.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><p class="eyebrow">Appointments</p><p style="font: var(--text-h3);">Your appointment with Nia</p></div><figcaption>An eyebrow that names the area the page belongs to.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><p class="eyebrow">Your HairPop</p><p style="font: var(--text-h3);">Reset your password</p></div><figcaption>The same "Your HairPop" eyebrow on every non-browsing screen, including sign in and errors, as the first mocks did; it stops carrying information.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p class="text-muted">Request HP-1048 · Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am · awaiting Nia’s reply.</p></div><figcaption>Put the facts the customer checks first in the subtitle.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p style="font: var(--text-h3);">Details</p></div><figcaption>Use a generic heading like "Details", as the first mocks' form panels did; it says nothing in a headings list.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Eyebrow|--color-fg-accent}}
      {{tok:Title|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Subtitle|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Eyebrow font|--text-overline}}
      {{tok:Eyebrow tracking|--letter-spacing-wide}}
      {{tok:Title font|--text-h1}}
      {{tok:Title size|--font-size-4xl}}
      {{tok:Title tracking|--letter-spacing-tight}}
      {{tok:Gaps: eyebrow / subtitle|--space-2|--space-1}}
      {{tok:Bottom margin|--space-6}}
      {{tok:Subtitle measure|--layout-measure}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;div class="page-header"&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
    &lt;p class="eyebrow"&gt;Appointments&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;h1 tabindex="-1"&gt;Your appointment with Nia&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;p class="subtitle"&gt;Request HP-1048 · Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am · awaiting Nia’s reply.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="page-header__actions"&gt;
    &lt;a class="btn" href="…"&gt;Request a change&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;a class="btn btn--primary" href="…"&gt;Message Nia&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.page-header</code></td><td>Wrapping row: title block and actions, 24px above the content.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.eyebrow</code></td><td>Accent overline above the title.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.subtitle</code></td><td>Muted line under the title.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.page-header__actions</code></td><td>Full width on phones with the primary full width; inline from 768px; hidden when empty.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>h1</code> inside <code>.page-header</code></td><td>Breaks long words at enlarged text; no focus ring when focused after navigation.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|"Discover" eyebrow}}
    {{mock:pages/appointment-detail/default|facts in the subtitle}}
    {{mock:pages/my-appointments/default|"Appointments" eyebrow and a page action}}
    {{mock:pages/sign-in/default|auth screen: no eyebrow}}
    {{mock:pages/not-found/default|error page: no eyebrow}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: every non-browsing screen, including sign in, legal and error pages, uses the eyebrow "Your HairPop" (system: the area name, or no eyebrow); form panels repeat a generic "Details" heading under a specific page title (system: name the section, such as "Your details"); the header had no slot for page actions (added <code>.page-header__actions</code>). The mocks now follow the eyebrow rule and show "Book a style" on My appointments. Added since: an empty actions container takes no space, long title words break at 200% text, and the focused title shows no ring.</p>
</section>
